  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Uma Maheswari vs State Rep. Through The on 11 June, 2024 Crl.O.P(MD).No. Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated : 11.06.2024 Coram : The Hon'Ble Mr Justice A.A.Nakkiran Crl.O.P(MD).No.14295 of 2020 and Crl.M.P(MD).No.6650 of 2020 Uma Maheswari ... Petit Vs. 1.State rep. through the Food Safety Officer, Madurai Corporation, Code No.572, O/o. the Designated Officer, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration, Viswanathapuram, Madurai 625 014. 2.Kamaraja 3.Prabaharan ... Respo Prayer:- Petition filed under Section 482 Cr.P.C., to call for the records in connection with the impugned charge sheet in STC.No.3550 2020 on the file of the Judicial Magistrate Court No.I, Madurai, Ma District and quash the same in so far as the petitioner is concerne For Petitioner : Mr.S. Sarvagan Prabhu For Respondent No.1 : Mr.R.M.Anbunithi Additional Public Prosecuto https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 1/7 Crl.O.P(MD ORDER on 11 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/48581387/ 1 Bhajan Whereas the prosecution under https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O.P(MD).No.14295 of 2020 Section 51 of Uma Maheswari vs State Rep. Through The on 11 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/48581387/ 2 the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 is without competency.",
    "facts": "Based on the complaint, case has been registered against the petitioner and other accused in STC.No. 3550 of 2020 on the file of the learned Judicial Magistrate No.I, Madurai for the offences under Sections 51 and 59(i) of the Food Safety and Standards Act,, 2006.",
    "arguments": "4. The learned Additional Public Prosecutor appearing for the first respondent would submit that the petitioner herein has been prosecuted under Section 59(i) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Crl.O.P(MD).No.14295 of 2020 2006, which is punishable with imprisonment under law. Since the complaint has been filed for prosecution under Section 51 of the Act as against the petitioner, it is his contention that the first respondent may be directed to initiate appropriate proceedings to hold an inquiry for the purpose of adjudicating the offences punishable under Section 51 of the Act by the Adjudicating Officer."
  },
